<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) & Pinet et al. (2019) Picasso tadpole craniofacial attractor remodeling (Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet)",
        "Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) & Pinet et al. (2019) Picasso tadpole craniofacial attractor remodeling faithfully reproduces Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py> ;
    schema:about "Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D finite-element cartilage biomechanics of Meckel's/palatoquadrate chondrocytes or explicit collagen-I fibril cleavage kinetics",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated PCA craniofacial axis, snout apex, 40-bin dorsal head width profile (r=0.9114), and bilateral dorsolateral eye detection (N=2 eyes, |Delta s|=0.0023) on xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Coupled 5-landmark Procrustes attractor ODE dx_i/dt = eta_MMP * [-K_i*(x_i - x_i^*) - sum_j C_ij*((x_i - x_j) - (x_i^* - x_j^*))] integrated via RK4 across NF stages 45->65 for 6 experimental regimes plus a 15x15 (alpha_pert, eta_MMP) morphospace grid",
        "reported_in_source: Pinet et al. (2019) Development 146:dev175893 thyroid-hormone-independent pre-metamorphic craniofacial remodeling and arrest under matrix metalloproteinase (MMP) inhibition (GM6001)",
        "reported_in_source: Proportional organ migration velocity scaling with displacement distance from target morphology (Vandenberg et al. 2012 Fig. 6) and restoration of bilateral facial symmetry",
        "reported_in_source: Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) Dev. Dyn. 241:863-878 craniofacial landmark tracking of eyes, nostrils/nares, and jaws across Nieuwkoop-Faber stages 45 to 65 showing goal-directed 'Picasso tadpole' normalization to froglet anatomy vs open-loop fixed-displacement vector failure",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal Procrustes craniofacial landmark coordinates (left/right eye, left/right naris, jaw midpoint) and reconstructed froglet head contour compared against dorsal Xenopus laevis specimen geometry" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2019-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap.py; output: docs/media/xenopus_craniofacial_remap_comparison.png; organism: Xenopus laevis African clawed frog tadpole and froglet; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: b508063893dc2ba283709bbd6f8bccfb0c0050e2d4a352a6be0037d6b7fbad04; artifact_sha256: a05e5ee5c81988c6442c768499a76a5f4e0a7ddae1b23bca3a0585f34a108cc2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/paper_citations.bib=f5f4d62c485aca75..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/scout_manifest.json=96534373d259eb28..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/xenopus_craniofacial_remap_reference.json=2656eaab51beb4ca..., datasets/xenopus_craniofacial_remap/xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg=8832f70a57f3d1c4...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Vandenberg, Adams & Levin (2012) Dev. Dyn. 241:863-878 craniofacial landmark tracking of eyes, nostrils/nares, and jaws across Nieuwkoop-Faber stages 45 to 65 showing goal-directed 'Picasso tadpole' normalization to froglet anatomy vs open-loop fixed-displacement vector failure | Proportional organ migration velocity scaling with displacement distance from target morphology (Vandenberg et al. 2012 Fig. 6) and restoration of bilateral facial symmetry | Pinet et al. (2019) Development 146:dev175893 thyroid-hormone-independent pre-metamorphic craniofacial remodeling and arrest under matrix metalloproteinase (MMP) inhibition (GM6001); reconstructed_in_script: Coupled 5-landmark Procrustes attractor ODE dx_i/dt = eta_MMP * [-K_i*(x_i - x_i^*) - sum_j C_ij*((x_i - x_j) - (x_i^* - x_j^*))] integrated via RK4 across NF stages 45->65 for 6 experimental regimes plus a 15x15 (alpha_pert, eta_MMP) morphospace grid | Automated PCA craniofacial axis, snout apex, 40-bin dorsal head width profile (r=0.9114), and bilateral dorsolateral eye detection (N=2 eyes, |Delta s|=0.0023) on xenopus_craniofacial_specimen.jpg; transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal Procrustes craniofacial landmark coordinates (left/right eye, left/right naris, jaw midpoint) and reconstructed froglet head contour compared against dorsal Xenopus laevis specimen geometry; does_not_claim: 3D finite-element cartilage biomechanics of Meckel's/palatoquadrate chondrocytes or explicit collagen-I fibril cleavage kinetics]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.23770>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2016.0555>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.073759>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.175893> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bischof-xenopus-craniofacial-remap-model-fidelity>,
